.TH DV_REPLAY 1 "2026-08-21" "diffvim 2.0" "diffvim scripts"
.SH NAME
dv_replay \- 
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dv_replay
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
NAME\fR
    dv_replay.sh — Replay a recorded animation\fR
\fR
SYNOPSIS\fR
    dv_replay.sh [-h|--help]\fR
    dv_replay.sh <oldfile> <recording.dv>\fR
\fR
DESCRIPTION\fR
    Replays a timed op stream previously recorded by dv_record.sh.\fR
    Loads the old file into the animator as the initial buffer, then\fR
    feeds the timed op stream through diffvim-animator-c (in\fR
    --no-display mode at speed 1000, with --snapshot) so that the\fR
    final buffer state is written to /tmp/dv_replay_out.txt.\fR
\fR
    This is the counterpart to dv_record.sh: the recording captures\fR
    the timed ops, and this script replays them.\fR
\fR
OPTIONS\fR
    -h, --help          Show this help message and exit 0.\fR
    <oldfile>           Path to the original/source file used as the\fR
                        initial buffer (same file passed to dv_record.sh).\fR
    <recording.dv>      Path to a recording file produced by dv_record.sh.\fR
\fR
EXAMPLES\fR
    dv_replay.sh examples/01_small_python/old.py /tmp/my_recording.dv\fR
        Replay the recording, writing the final buffer to\fR
        /tmp/dv_replay_out.txt.\fR
\fR
    dv_record.sh old.py new.py /tmp/my_recording.dv\fR
        (Companion command) record the animation first.\fR
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show detailed help and exit
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR diffvim (1)
